@domain:repository-scanning @area:skipped-files @from:gradebook-code/base
Feature: Recognising generated and minified files
  Lets a maintainer trust that the score reflects code someone writes by hand, not protobuf stubs, bundles or other machine output.

  Background:
    Given a repository containing source files in a recognised language

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.001 @rule:scanning.generated.skipped-by-file-name @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/base.py#is_generated @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_recognised @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_excluded_from_the_score
  Scenario Outline: A file named like generated output is skipped
    Given a source file named "<file>"
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then "<file>" is not scored
    And it is counted among the generated files skipped

    Examples:
      | file                |
      | app.min.js          |
      | api.pb.go           |
      | model_pb2.py        |
      | model_pb2_grpc.py   |
      | thing.g.dart        |
      | client.generated.ts |
      | schema_generated.go |

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.002 @rule:scanning.generated.skipped-by-header-marker @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/base.py#is_generated @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_recognised @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_excluded_from_the_score
  Scenario Outline: A file declaring itself generated near its top is skipped
    Given a source file "wire.go" whose opening text contains "<marker>"
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then "wire.go" is not scored
    And the report says how many generated file(s) were skipped

    Examples:
      | marker                                    |
      | @generated                                |
      | Code generated by protoc. DO NOT EDIT.    |
      | autogenerated                             |
      | auto-generated                            |
      | generated by the protocol buffer compiler |
      | @dart=2.12                                |
      | machine generated                         |

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.003 @rule:scanning.generated.marker-only-near-top @inferred @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/base.py#is_generated
  Scenario: A generated marker deep inside a file does not skip it
    Given a source file whose first 2000 characters are ordinary code
    And the words "DO NOT EDIT" appear only after that
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then the file is scored
    And it is not counted among the generated files skipped

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.004 @rule:scanning.generated.minified-line-skips @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/base.py#is_generated @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_generated_files_are_recognised @questionable
  Scenario Outline: A file with a line over 500 characters in its first 50 lines is treated as minified and skipped
    Given a source file "bundle.js" with a <length>-character line at line <line>
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then "bundle.js" is <outcome>

    Examples:
      | length | line | outcome              |
      | 1600   | 1    | skipped as generated |
      | 501    | 50   | skipped as generated |
      | 500    | 1    | scored               |
      | 2000   | 51   | scored               |

  @id:gradebook-code.repository-scanning.skipped-files.005 @rule:scanning.generated.handwritten-kept @verified @source:gradebook-code/gradebook_code/base.py#is_generated @test:gradebook-code/tests/test_gradebook_code.py#test_handwritten_files_are_not_skipped
  Scenario Outline: Hand-written code is scored even when its name mentions generating
    Given a source file "<file>" with ordinary short lines and no generated marker
    When the operator grades the repository
    Then "<file>" is scored
    And it is not counted among the generated files skipped

    Examples:
      | file         |
      | billing.py   |
      | generator.py |
